# L §5.5 ('the axis id in a key position reads the input at the current option, and fans out') and E §3.1 step 8 /
# E §3.3: an ask fans out over every axis its evaluation reads, the axis that picks a leg's place included. gift
# books amt = 10.00 PLN from world to pln[payee[spouse]]: pln[ana] under first, pln[ben] under second. So
# flows(pln[p], 2026) (L §5.14.3: movements into x minus those out) is 10.00 PLN for the place the option names and
# 0.00 PLN for the other, directly in the ask (q) and through a def (n). (Was: 0.00 PLN for both, with no fan-out:
# the move's refusal was left out of a place's flows in silence; a fault found by running a text.)
=== m.tally
model p13
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-18
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "synthetic"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

axis spouse
  first "the first reading"
  second "the second reading"

index people = [ana, ben]

place pln[p in people]: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..

input payee[o in spouse]: key people
input amt: money PLN
input pay_day: date
input yr: year

move gift: transfers
  on pay_day
  leg cash from world to pln[payee[spouse]] amount amt

def net_flow[p in people]: money PLN = flows(pln[p], yr)

ask n: net_flow[p] for p in people law 2026-06-30
ask q: flows(pln[p], 2026) for p in people law 2026-06-30

version v1
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  payee[first] = ana
  payee[second] = ben
  amt = 10.00 PLN
  pay_day = 2026-03-01
  yr = 2026
  opening[pln[ana]] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
  opening[pln[ben]] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
=== expect
n (p = ana) [spouse = first]: 10.00 PLN
...
n (p = ana) [spouse = second]: 0.00 PLN
...
n (p = ben) [spouse = first]: 0.00 PLN
...
n (p = ben) [spouse = second]: 10.00 PLN
...
q (p = ana) [spouse = first]: 10.00 PLN
...
q (p = ana) [spouse = second]: 0.00 PLN
...
q (p = ben) [spouse = first]: 0.00 PLN
...
q (p = ben) [spouse = second]: 10.00 PLN
...
